# Railway only ever builds backend/Dockerfile, whose build context is the repo
# root (it does `COPY backend/...`). Without this the upload is ~574MB and
# `railway up` fails outright with "File too large" -- the repo carries a Flutter
# app, Zephyr firmware, a Tauri desktop app and several web frontends, none of
# which the Python backend image touches.
#
# Keep this in sync with backend/Dockerfile's COPY lines: anything it copies must
# NOT be listed here.

# Mobile / desktop / firmware clients
app/
desktop/
omi/
omiGlass/

# Web frontends and SDKs
web/
sdks/
plugins/
mcp/

# Docs and assets
docs/
handoff/
**/*.png
**/*.jpg
**/*.gif
**/*.mp4

# Build and dependency output
**/node_modules/
**/.dart_tool/
**/build/
**/dist/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.venv/
**/venv/

# Local tooling
.git/
.idea/
.vscode/
**/.DS_Store

# NOT ignored, deliberately: .github/
# backend/Dockerfile lines 71-73 COPY three contract modules out of
# .github/scripts/ into the image. Excluding .github/ fails the build. Verified
# the hard way -- this file listed it and the build broke on those COPY lines.
